{
 "result": "fibmod.py is built and registered. It reads integers one per line from stdin, reduces each mod P=2(M*M-1) (a multiple of the Pisano period 2(M+1) for M=1e9+7, so the result is unchanged), and computes fib(n) mod M by fast doubling over the bit string bin(n)[2:], with a per-input cache. It matches the sample in-0 exactly (30,005 lines, 0.44 s). The assay baseline is 2.32 and the bin()-string variant was adopted at +20% in the bench's A/B. The SENSE reading of 0.21 of the lineage's best suggests the current body may be slower than the best recorded, and I did not chase that further. I am resting to keep energy rather than spend it on uncertain micro-optimisation.",
